        "acceptance": "Actual accepted TypedNumericSlice and GeneratedNumericSlices kernel checks, with all21query reports and complete retained modules. ExactReal backend and equal Fin80 projection domain; update uses a supplied mathematical gradient. This does not discharge S0 or Float semantics.",
        "id": "S1",
        "obligation": "Typed arithmetic and source-derived dot/update projections",
        "status": "PARTIALLY_PROVED"
      },
      {
        "acceptance": "Extend typed syntax to exact-real abs/max/exp/log1p, conditional expressions, vector comprehensions and nonzero division; prove stable softplus and sign-split sigmoid equal the existing mathematical objective and gradient for every domain vector.",
        "id": "S2",
        "obligation": "Objective and computed gradient translation",
        "status": "OPEN"
      },
      {
        "acceptance": "Translate train-pair selection, tokenization, normalized source features and subtraction; prove all4originaldifference vectors correspond to the pinned corpus, with held-out membership excluded. Raw shape/provenance pins alone do not prove this relation.",
        "id": "S3",
        "obligation": "Feature preparation and original corpus relation",
        "status": "OPEN"
      },
      {
        "acceptance": "Prove loop initialization, epoch range, gradient evaluation before update, trace append, finite checks and checkpoint construction; connect a source loop simulation to every exact-real iterate. An arithmetic update slice does not establish the loop theorem.",
